  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "07",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p07-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "b42f37234312ee7268c549b819e131af03f98f045905ce597a5b3888176ef0c5",
        "2": "3d4174e0f219a837d7221a678c241548339fc2e7a7c1f8824bc253d329002f47",
        "3": "eb8629d6bfbceb007968c4f50f65470cbe73f008ce7836713203c5690a17441c"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s01-c1-a5607017771d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The new release is unhealthy. To roll back, you need the exact image that ran before, not whatever a familiar tag points to now. Record the deployed digest with the release.",
          "text_sha256": "a5607017771db77113ba3234e503f89c792703a63a2b0504b82f9c1718d402fc",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a5607017771db77113ba3234e503f89c792703a63a2b0504b82f9c1718d402fc",
          "asset_sha256": "b42f37234312ee7268c549b819e131af03f98f045905ce597a5b3888176ef0c5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s01-c2-8670888cbb91",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Keep the known-good manifest and its dependent artifacts, including the applicable architectures. Retaining a release label isn't enough if you can't pull the image that label names.",
          "text_sha256": "8670888cbb91276c9903b839e64f942d54a7d49f0b726eaef5728839923798e2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8670888cbb91276c9903b839e64f942d54a7d49f0b726eaef5728839923798e2",
          "asset_sha256": "b42f37234312ee7268c549b819e131af03f98f045905ce597a5b3888176ef0c5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s01-c3-26c074ce96a5",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Preview the lifecycle rule and check which images it would expire. Protect the approved rollback versions and confirm you can still pull them before enabling cleanup.",
          "text_sha256": "26c074ce96a5ea0665ee4218f8961d5648f2dca6cf612c8ba57e3e1307730fb1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "26c074ce96a5ea0665ee4218f8961d5648f2dca6cf612c8ba57e3e1307730fb1",
          "asset_sha256": "b42f37234312ee7268c549b819e131af03f98f045905ce597a5b3888176ef0c5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s02-c1-1a05fee6c910",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A second Region needs the image. Configure replication to its registry, push an eligible image, and compare the destination digest. This moves the image artifacts, not the running service.",
          "text_sha256": "1a05fee6c910494dc5bc39a1e9c545a7f457f0de4ac62553c91e2e419acf15be",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1a05fee6c910494dc5bc39a1e9c545a7f457f0de4ac62553c91e2e419acf15be",
          "asset_sha256": "3d4174e0f219a837d7221a678c241548339fc2e7a7c1f8824bc253d329002f47"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s02-c2-dc5563e3dd94",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the image was already in the source before replication, it does not move automatically. Run replication backfill for eligible images that match the existing rule and verify the destination copy.",
          "text_sha256": "dc5563e3dd9463463905be2a30740fa74bf6d0e422c9f2d21f7a5f7c7902459d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dc5563e3dd9463463905be2a30740fa74bf6d0e422c9f2d21f7a5f7c7902459d",
          "asset_sha256": "3d4174e0f219a837d7221a678c241548339fc2e7a7c1f8824bc253d329002f47"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s02-c3-e6f50da5587f",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The new registry still needs its own access and settings. The application still needs deployment configuration, a working network path, and a runtime that can pull that image.",
          "text_sha256": "e6f50da5587f1d17118544571876a3fce79845f5c666968acf3399407934166b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e6f50da5587f1d17118544571876a3fce79845f5c666968acf3399407934166b",
          "asset_sha256": "3d4174e0f219a837d7221a678c241548339fc2e7a7c1f8824bc253d329002f47"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s03-c1-e44a483011c5",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An image scan finds a package issue. Basic scanning covers supported operating-system package vulnerabilities. Decide whether scan-on-push or manual scanning meets your needs.",
          "text_sha256": "e44a483011c575fbc2e160f3113770174f6142506bf953e2de16678d2b1033dd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e44a483011c575fbc2e160f3113770174f6142506bf953e2de16678d2b1033dd",
          "asset_sha256": "eb8629d6bfbceb007968c4f50f65470cbe73f008ce7836713203c5690a17441c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s03-c2-a5e3cc186913",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Enhanced scanning uses Amazon Inspector for supported operating-system and programming-language packages. Continuous scanning can surface findings after an image was pushed.",
          "text_sha256": "a5e3cc1869139837c17df128d434181628d7388f2dd3d209a8dfaba257e2a221",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a5e3cc1869139837c17df128d434181628d7388f2dd3d209a8dfaba257e2a221",
          "asset_sha256": "eb8629d6bfbceb007968c4f50f65470cbe73f008ce7836713203c5690a17441c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p07-andrew-exp-s03-c3-81583b4c7e23",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Triage whether the finding affects the workload, then rebuild from fixed components. Scan the new digest and deploy that exact image. A clean report is not proof that an old image is safe.",
          "text_sha256": "81583b4c7e2356dc92a7960ba2112196d69067e4046617f7b4bbc42358669e86",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "81583b4c7e2356dc92a7960ba2112196d69067e4046617f7b4bbc42358669e86",
          "asset_sha256": "eb8629d6bfbceb007968c4f50f65470cbe73f008ce7836713203c5690a17441c"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "08",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p08-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "4db14b8367577380a2bcd43a4115d2ac57dbe3c978e8add7e106aea2316b23d5",
        "2": "0bd2c59220dde57948ebbde54c066110d0c49ec116862278d6cb826a52dbff80",
        "3": "35d753f6b9bce1cf96375a09fcff428c3b530f038d64d0ff2326a978b850f3af"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s01-c1-498bde85019b",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "E K S gives the application a koo ber NET ees A P I without the team running the control plane. The control plane manages the cluster, but it is not where the application process runs.",
          "text_sha256": "498bde85019b48e43a9116fdb139c220367afa3a32c85dd362457a0a42bfbfe6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "00d73c6248517d78d02f16bc6d22b5644812e065eeb0ad1d399028d84626ce70",
          "asset_sha256": "4db14b8367577380a2bcd43a4115d2ac57dbe3c978e8add7e106aea2316b23d5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s01-c2-65f632704f81",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Pick a worker model, then use a deployment to run Pods. A Service gives clients a stable way to reach them. Identity, storage and networking still need design.",
          "text_sha256": "65f632704f816763878b70bd721b39350d0958b98d9848e20763fd74916ef907",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "65f632704f816763878b70bd721b39350d0958b98d9848e20763fd74916ef907",
          "asset_sha256": "4db14b8367577380a2bcd43a4115d2ac57dbe3c978e8add7e106aea2316b23d5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s02-c1-db5a7dff050c",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The managed control plane spans Availability Zones inside one Region. Your tools reach the koo ber NET ees A P I there. That makes the A P I resilient within its design, not the application by default.",
          "text_sha256": "db5a7dff050cf4cd322f552cf5a04b4ce061cd8bcf036aba27d39953124214be",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "587fb934a2a5fff81af28085a5a25157e081b0f86f8f71a9315dda17bb3d4d10",
          "asset_sha256": "0bd2c59220dde57948ebbde54c066110d0c49ec116862278d6cb826a52dbff80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s02-c2-aca100f74c6f",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the app runs only one Pod, a managed control plane doesn't make a second copy. Plan replicas and placement, plus networking, storage and workload updates. For another Region, design a separate cluster and traffic plan.",
          "text_sha256": "aca100f74c6f14d738c0c077a343dc3a8b0b48d4fc6954993a22da2c01cb9189",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "aca100f74c6f14d738c0c077a343dc3a8b0b48d4fc6954993a22da2c01cb9189",
          "asset_sha256": "0bd2c59220dde57948ebbde54c066110d0c49ec116862278d6cb826a52dbff80"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s03-c1-19057958215e",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A managed node group helps with E C two node lifecycle. You still size capacity and validate application health. With self-managed nodes, your team takes on more bootstrap, patch and upgrade work.",
          "text_sha256": "19057958215ef391b6c93813abd4270b78b254c3f0f48a1903bd58fc4966658a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c1fc5c0beaceeccdec5ef3738d8afc92408a1cefb616fc1e3746b0d4378344a0",
          "asset_sha256": "35d753f6b9bce1cf96375a09fcff428c3b530f038d64d0ff2326a978b850f3af"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s03-c2-832b1757a4bc",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Fargate runs matching Pods without a worker-node fleet you administer. Confirm the Pod fits its constraints before choosing it.",
          "text_sha256": "832b1757a4bc58922b78f8b3543352f0d64cd1c5b58f9c145edceb47ee15aa40",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "832b1757a4bc58922b78f8b3543352f0d64cd1c5b58f9c145edceb47ee15aa40",
          "asset_sha256": "35d753f6b9bce1cf96375a09fcff428c3b530f038d64d0ff2326a978b850f3af"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p08-andrew-exp-s03-c3-7879a80b27fb",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Auto Mode manages node compute and selected platform functions. Check where the workload needs more control or uses a feature that the mode cannot provide.",
          "text_sha256": "7879a80b27fbe16d4d4770731bc96f9fc56251872780f916b2cab6bc7a3d5307",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7879a80b27fbe16d4d4770731bc96f9fc56251872780f916b2cab6bc7a3d5307",
          "asset_sha256": "35d753f6b9bce1cf96375a09fcff428c3b530f038d64d0ff2326a978b850f3af"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "09",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p09-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "f516e14bc31fb4ddd0c4cf4c5cdb59f2649f51321533778edbaa926e916c6a61",
        "2": "ce1bc95ee9755f2a2e9ed5ecb5da1d3589cd7622b1b24efbef2d04886aa56b9f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p09-andrew-exp-s01-c1-9522508eefa9",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The public load balancer receives internet requests. It can still send them to application targets on private workers. Public ingress does not require giving each Pod a public address.",
          "text_sha256": "9522508eefa9e6019033faacb197c3d10412eb64cd0040f3c8866b6c422aadf0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9522508eefa9e6019033faacb197c3d10412eb64cd0040f3c8866b6c422aadf0",
          "asset_sha256": "f516e14bc31fb4ddd0c4cf4c5cdb59f2649f51321533778edbaa926e916c6a61"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p09-andrew-exp-s01-c2-1c692a271be8",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Trace the independent paths the workers need, such as the cluster A P I, image pulls and log delivery. Choose appropriate endpoints or controlled egress. The load balancer does not provide those outbound paths.",
          "text_sha256": "1c692a271be8e8994c4c2140189b14c92c4819895410786097390a3330c6f8c8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f326b067505598d4e3a9faca55cd7299e02c895a9b43e3aa748475b64f72e8eb",
          "asset_sha256": "f516e14bc31fb4ddd0c4cf4c5cdb59f2649f51321533778edbaa926e916c6a61"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p09-andrew-exp-s01-c3-a0b245c58fe6",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Check subnet placement, target type, security rules and health checks. Prove a real request reaches the private app target and that the health check uses the intended path.",
          "text_sha256": "a0b245c58fe676a1c45bbfb2d9c7b7c2a705f00c85560b595446965e23e68d24",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a0b245c58fe676a1c45bbfb2d9c7b7c2a705f00c85560b595446965e23e68d24",
          "asset_sha256": "f516e14bc31fb4ddd0c4cf4c5cdb59f2649f51321533778edbaa926e916c6a61"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p09-andrew-exp-s02-c1-8492faff9471",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A developer entering the cluster must first authenticate and then be authorized for the koo ber NET ees action. Use the configured cluster-access path and enforce the appropriate namespace and object permissions. Being signed in does not grant every koo ber NET ees action.",
          "text_sha256": "8492faff9471e4e5543a53b46c3d207efe7e6bc6db28a87eb389ae2344883880",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d49b1b4cbb28196415022faad61c689d4b5b03c5f6b86876c7944b3a997c35c2",
          "asset_sha256": "ce1bc95ee9755f2a2e9ed5ecb5da1d3589cd7622b1b24efbef2d04886aa56b9f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p09-andrew-exp-s02-c2-caadde459d7a",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "An application Pod calling S three needs a different permission. Associate its service account with a scoped role using supported Pod Identity or ear sah. koo ber NET ees permission to list Pods does not grant S three access.",
          "text_sha256": "caadde459d7afcad39585e06354d5c2f964837930557653a6b01cb027afff409",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4aac80426fe6c544f84f358797db41674043052dbb8910bd372c1ed05ce7408b",
          "asset_sha256": "ce1bc95ee9755f2a2e9ed5ecb5da1d3589cd7622b1b24efbef2d04886aa56b9f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p09-andrew-exp-s02-c3-a7a236b945e3",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Pod Identity is not supported on Fargate; use a supported method such as ear sah there. A broad node role is not a substitute for permissions limited to the workload.",
          "text_sha256": "a7a236b945e3af83ffee587302946562096e4352e2d47816d655dfea77bcb0a1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1a676ba1571bfe146c82b976c40b83716e1536e3ffd87686728f220c432dd30f",
          "asset_sha256": "ce1bc95ee9755f2a2e9ed5ecb5da1d3589cd7622b1b24efbef2d04886aa56b9f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "10",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p10-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "db3133b02971546e5d2b06d20a6cfd46ba8a079b487a446de87b6247a9559bd3",
        "2": "c3046869200942aec1c374d614b8387e673743dec74e3e87f8eb9125ad6fd797"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s01-c1-2160b5739959",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The Pod asks for storage through a claim. The storage class selects the provisioner or the claim can bind to a matching volume. A claim alone does not make that storage compatible with the Pod.",
          "text_sha256": "2160b57399599bacaa00e5a8deea51d246a0720d6422c7e014269db17a94cce0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2160b57399599bacaa00e5a8deea51d246a0720d6422c7e014269db17a94cce0",
          "asset_sha256": "db3133b02971546e5d2b06d20a6cfd46ba8a079b487a446de87b6247a9559bd3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s01-c2-5e28b733cb10",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For a block volume, the E B S C S I path must place the Pod where it can attach the volume in its zone. This is not shared multi-zone file storage, and E B S volumes do not mount to Fargate Pods.",
          "text_sha256": "5e28b733cb10508b3fdaf344422f7700542dbed28357b9aa0497726072dd2af6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b2418a9f9167ae096c4e6d9bdc48b1c5cc98adc01d5246a54fea6b4a53b64e7a",
          "asset_sha256": "db3133b02971546e5d2b06d20a6cfd46ba8a079b487a446de87b6247a9559bd3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s01-c3-1b18e86f94e9",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For shared file access across supported compute, consider E F S and its mount paths. E K S Fargate can use static E F S provisioning, not dynamic persistent-volume provisioning.",
          "text_sha256": "1b18e86f94e950ff55390906eac6d3bddafaa1a3a4714c33cee8d0fc94b18251",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0df990ec71706425c724781bba12710f2051dc4369d4bc0798a179ee8a91a46b",
          "asset_sha256": "db3133b02971546e5d2b06d20a6cfd46ba8a079b487a446de87b6247a9559bd3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s01-c4-26051f2b7b47",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Access modes and reclaim policy decide how volumes are used and what happens to their data when a claim is removed. Test the mount and the retention outcome you expect.",
          "text_sha256": "26051f2b7b4757190eb32e418bb2f7f49ff2655e5960dd3ab96ebb3e09f3239e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "26051f2b7b4757190eb32e418bb2f7f49ff2655e5960dd3ab96ebb3e09f3239e",
          "asset_sha256": "db3133b02971546e5d2b06d20a6cfd46ba8a079b487a446de87b6247a9559bd3"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s02-c1-2a8fa517b1ea",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For the parallel file workload, check the F S x for Lustre C S I driver and the nodes that will mount it. The point is to expose the filesystem contract the application actually expects.",
          "text_sha256": "2a8fa517b1eaf349476404f3358b920b07fbc65d0d906d3928e1785cb1dcb448",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "401334cae51b4f04f0b9f4b23f8044be2f0a9049993dfbba7813fd33fe3f5fda",
          "asset_sha256": "c3046869200942aec1c374d614b8387e673743dec74e3e87f8eb9125ad6fd797"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s02-c2-a4fbe4564bd5",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the workload instead needs eligible on tap storage, check its supported Trident integration and protocol. An F S x filesystem existing in the account does not mean any Pod can mount it.",
          "text_sha256": "a4fbe4564bd5207cdefb54445f617f1d8780139c766e93749e5a4d2c1423302e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9d30343c56691c9fa8eb450e0b5bf6dc75fb743111426e3e1320f8e766a51ffa",
          "asset_sha256": "c3046869200942aec1c374d614b8387e673743dec74e3e87f8eb9125ad6fd797"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p10-andrew-exp-s02-c3-a885892d34c2",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Check node and platform support, permissions, routes, storage class and reclaim policy. Mount from an actual Pod and validate access and recovery. Do not assume support on every Fargate or node combination.",
          "text_sha256": "a885892d34c2e5232b6596e979ae521b58d26fe3ca93be85286ae656665b43e7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a885892d34c2e5232b6596e979ae521b58d26fe3ca93be85286ae656665b43e7",
          "asset_sha256": "c3046869200942aec1c374d614b8387e673743dec74e3e87f8eb9125ad6fd797"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "11",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p11-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "6a98f4ce7ac1a29af0b74e50ec678a242fe9d998783108b3a6a17bd0a7fa4ede",
        "2": "0b1fa527209c123da7be057ddd4aa68f09745aa54fee74326c29303aed1f3ece"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s01-c1-63b7c9b82ac5",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Load rises and the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler raises desired replicas. That creates more Pods to schedule. It does not itself add a worker.",
          "text_sha256": "63b7c9b82ac5a89c18dc1a13fa014103e3783a789b7a632715ce319d482b9c50",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "63b7c9b82ac5a89c18dc1a13fa014103e3783a789b7a632715ce319d482b9c50",
          "asset_sha256": "6a98f4ce7ac1a29af0b74e50ec678a242fe9d998783108b3a6a17bd0a7fa4ede"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s01-c2-3fb72dad846d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the new Pods don't fit, a compatible node autoscaler can add capacity. Check resource requests, placement rules and quotas, because waiting Pods do not always mean you just need more nodes.",
          "text_sha256": "3fb72dad846d2b45c00bf953e19035755f2a794db6322a67b2d792433f486c47",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3fb72dad846d2b45c00bf953e19035755f2a794db6322a67b2d792433f486c47",
          "asset_sha256": "6a98f4ce7ac1a29af0b74e50ec678a242fe9d998783108b3a6a17bd0a7fa4ede"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s01-c3-72691d776410",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Four Pods are not four separate failure domains. Verify that ready replicas actually spread across the desired zones and that termination and disruption behavior match the design.",
          "text_sha256": "72691d7764102fbacf195bc8e42ed0896d9851711a7a90bb6ede97bf24fce7b9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "72691d7764102fbacf195bc8e42ed0896d9851711a7a90bb6ede97bf24fce7b9",
          "asset_sha256": "6a98f4ce7ac1a29af0b74e50ec678a242fe9d998783108b3a6a17bd0a7fa4ede"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s02-c1-26157a1e074e",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The load balancer reports an unhealthy target. Check target health, then compare the Service or Ingress events to see whether the intended Pod is actually behind that route.",
          "text_sha256": "26157a1e074e71c2d5a53f41d19c948224565b73fca29fd0b4087b3e03a3b5a5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "26157a1e074e71c2d5a53f41d19c948224565b73fca29fd0b4087b3e03a3b5a5",
          "asset_sha256": "0b1fa527209c123da7be057ddd4aa68f09745aa54fee74326c29303aed1f3ece"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s02-c2-6beb6bdb7a61",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Now check whether the Pod is ready and what it logged. A running container can still fail to answer the health-check path.",
          "text_sha256": "6beb6bdb7a612428173ad5c2027416ef637ad6e67932ed0770c32aa1ff630260",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6beb6bdb7a612428173ad5c2027416ef637ad6e67932ed0770c32aa1ff630260",
          "asset_sha256": "0b1fa527209c123da7be057ddd4aa68f09745aa54fee74326c29303aed1f3ece"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s02-c3-8d15ad82ad56",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If several Pods fail on the same node, inspect resource and container metrics. For an A P I or scheduling issue, use available control-plane evidence. Control-plane logs must be enabled where needed.",
          "text_sha256": "8d15ad82ad569574ed1d18f806b87208b1f3a5229812ab5224d267a4f6aea760",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bb2e24525283bf0459ad0f2dddc72e118ac269f3f5b54e5a7741efd5284a70b1",
          "asset_sha256": "0b1fa527209c123da7be057ddd4aa68f09745aa54fee74326c29303aed1f3ece"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p11-andrew-exp-s02-c4-1ed43cc46b15",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Metrics show trends, logs describe failures, events track transitions, and traces follow requests. Connect those clues to the same failing request. Container Insights requires configuration.",
          "text_sha256": "1ed43cc46b1566390db20aa9335789f50b60f0c3e1fca558205411723bf523ac",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "1ed43cc46b1566390db20aa9335789f50b60f0c3e1fca558205411723bf523ac",
          "asset_sha256": "0b1fa527209c123da7be057ddd4aa68f09745aa54fee74326c29303aed1f3ece"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
